Package: netimpute
Type: Package
Title: Node-Level Network Measures as Predictors for Multiple Imputation
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person(
      "Jane", "Doe",
      email = "jane@example.com",
      role = c("aut", "cre")
    )
  )
Description: Computes node-level social network measures (degree, reciprocity,
    centrality, brokerage, closure, and attribute-scale-appropriate homophily
    measures) across one or more networks sharing a common attribute schema,
    and reduces them to principal components usable as auxiliary predictors
    in a multiple-imputation model (e.g. mice with predictive mean matching),
    while optionally preserving specific raw measures un-transformed when
    they are themselves part of a substantive hypothesis. Also provides a
    dyadic (cell-level) regression for network ties - an MR-QAP-style model
    without the permutation test, since the goal is prediction rather than
    inference - and a mice-style chained-equations routine, netmice(), that
    jointly imputes missing nodal attributes and missing network ties.
